<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>Internet Download Speed Test</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<P><SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; FONT-FAMILY: Roboto, sans-serif; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(32,33,36); FONT-STYLE: normal; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(248,249,250); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial">This&nbsp;task&nbsp;finds the latitude and longitude of&nbsp;a machine&nbsp;to find the closest </SPAN><A style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Roboto, sans-serif; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; BACKGROUND: rgb(248,249,250); WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(26,115,232); PADDING-BOTTOM: 0px; FONT-STYLE: normal; PADDING-TOP: 0px; PADDING-LEFT: 0px; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; MARGIN: 0px; LETTER-SPACING: normal; PADDING-RIGHT: 0px; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent" href="http://speedtest.net/" rel="noopener nofollow noreferrer" target=_blank>speedtest.net</A><SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; FONT-FAMILY: Roboto, sans-serif; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(32,33,36); FONT-STYLE: normal; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(248,249,250); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial"> servers. <BR>It then sorts the servers removing duplicate companies and then by distance. <BR>It then hits the closest servers and downloads a 25Mb file 12 times for each server (just like </SPAN><A style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Roboto, sans-serif; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; BACKGROUND: rgb(248,249,250); WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(26,115,232); PADDING-BOTTOM: 0px; FONT-STYLE: normal; PADDING-TOP: 0px; PADDING-LEFT: 0px; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; MARGIN: 0px; LETTER-SPACING: normal; PADDING-RIGHT: 0px; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent" href="http://speedtest.net/" rel="noopener nofollow noreferrer" target=_blank>speedtest.net</A><SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; FONT-FAMILY: Roboto, sans-serif; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(32,33,36); FONT-STYLE: normal; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(248,249,250); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial">) and calculates the average download speed. It does this for 8 servers (I chose 8 to have a bigger data set when comparing speeds).<BR></SPAN><SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; FONT-FAMILY: Roboto, sans-serif; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(32,33,36); FONT-STYLE: normal; ORPHANS: 2; WIDOWS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(248,249,250); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial">It will then find the fastest speed of the 8 servers&nbsp;and saves it to a file on the computer that can later be read by a bigfix analysis.</SPAN></P>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>true</Relevance>
    <Category>BigFix.me</Category>
